# Build output
# Note: unanchored, because the Gradle module sits at com.smccloud.hotdeath/app --
# an "app/release/" pattern would only match at the repo root.
build/
release/
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.aar
*.dex
*.class
bin/
gen/
out/
proguard/

# Gradle
.gradle/
.kotlin/

# Local configuration -- contains an absolute SDK path, machine-specific
local.properties

# Credential stores. The CI clients themselves are tracked -- Jenkinsfile,
# jenkins.sh and jenkins.ps1 -- because a controller URL is only a default that
# the environment or a creds file overrides, and none of the three embeds a
# token. These three DO, so they must never be committed:
#
#   jenkins-creds.xml  the Jenkins API token, DPAPI-encrypted to one user on one
#                      machine, which is also why it is useless to anyone else
#   jenkins-creds      the same token in plaintext KEY=VALUE form, which is what
#                      the bash client reads
#   github-creds.xml   a GitHub token, DPAPI-encrypted the same way. Needs write
#                      access to releases, since publishing means uploading an
#                      APK to a tag
/jenkins-creds.xml
/jenkins-creds

# A GitHub token, stored the same way: DPAPI-encrypted to this user on this
# machine, written by a one-liner the maintainer runs once. It needs write
# access to releases to upload an APK to a tag, which is why it cannot be a
# read-only token and why it is worth keeping out of git rather than in it.
/github-creds.xml

# Signing material. These must never be committed.
*.jks
*.keystore
# The properties file next to them: four plaintext passwords. It has no
# extension, so neither rule above covers it, and it looks like ordinary
# configuration -- which is what makes it the one most likely to be committed by
# accident. Unanchored, because it lives in the Gradle module at
# com.smccloud.hotdeath/app/, not at the repo root.
keystore.properties
# Android Studio's "export signing config" writes an encrypted copy beside the
# key. Same secrets, different extension.
*.properties.asc

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml
.navigation/
captures/
.externalNativeBuild
.cxx/
.vscode/

# Logs and profiling
*.log
*.hprof

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Merge and editor leftovers
*.orig
*.rej
*.swp
*~

# Rasterised card art: build output from artwork/cards/render_card_pngs.py. The
# SVGs beside it are the checked-in source, so committing 425 generated PNGs on top
# of them would duplicate the source and put every one of them in the diff when a
# face changes.
artwork/cards/png/
